      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "(A)\n\n1) Tasters are TT and Tt. Non-tasters are tt.\n2) Frequency of non-tasters: q² = 1 - 0.604 = 0.396.\n3) Allele frequency t: q = √0.396 ≈ 0.629.\n4) Allele frequency T: p = 1 - q = 0.371.\n5) Genotype frequencies:\n   - TT: p² = 0.371² ≈ 0.1376 → 0.1376 × 798 ≈ 109.\n   - Tt: 2pq = 2·0.371·0.629 ≈ 0.4666 → 0.4666 × 798 ≈ 373.\n   - tt: q² = 0.3960 → 0.3960 × 798 ≈ 316.\n6) Check: 109+373+316 = 798.\n\nAnswer: (A)<channel|>Answer: (A)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2833",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "H",
      "got": "H",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "a) Sense strand: 5' TAC CTT TAA GCA TTT GTT TCT TCT TCT 3' (complementary to antisense, same sequence as mRNA).\nb) mRNA: 5' AUG GAU AAA GUU UUA AAC AGA GAG GAA UCU 3' (transcribed from sense strand).\nc) Translation: AUG→Met, GAU→Asp, AAA→Lys, GUU→Val, UUA→Leu, AAC→Asn, AGA→Arg, GAG→Glu, GAA→Glu, UCU→Ser.\nThe sequence is 10 codons long. Option H matches all three parts correctly.\n\nAnswer: (H)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2834",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "G",
      "got": "G",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The woman's father was colorblind (X^c X^c), so she must carry one recessive allele (X^c X^c or X^c X^C). Since she herself has normal vision, she must be a carrier: X^c X^C. The man has normal vision, so his genotype is X^C Y. The cross X^c X^C × X^C Y gives four possible offspring genotypes: X^C X^C, X^c X^C, X^C Y, X^c Y. Of these four equally likely outcomes, two are female (X^C X^C, X^c X^C) and two are male (X^C Y, X^c Y). A male offspring is colorblind only if it inherits the X^c allele from its mother, which happens in 1/2 of the male cases. Since males make up 1/2 of all offspring, the overall probability of any child being colorblind is 1/2 × 1/2 = 1/4.\n\nAnswer: (G)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2835",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "E",
      "got": "H",
      "ok": false,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The recombination frequency is calculated as the ratio of recombinant plaques to total plaques, multiplied by 100. The total number of plaques is 44. The number of recombinant plaques is the difference between the number of plaques on strain B (40) and the number on strain K (4), which is 36. The recombination frequency is (36/44) × 100 ≈ 8.18%. This value is the proportion of progeny that resulted from a crossover event between the two mutation sites.\n\nAnswer: (H)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2836",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "H",
      "got": "A",
      "ok": false,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The allele frequencies are p = 0.62 and q = 0.38. Hardy-Weinberg proportions are p² (MM), 2pq (MN), and q² (NN).\n1) MM: 0.62² × 610 ≈ 238.34 → 238\n2) MN: 2·0.62·0.38 × 610 ≈ 292.68 → 293 (zaokrouhleno na nejbližší celé číslo)\n3) NN: 0.38² × 610 ≈ 87.96 → 88\nKontrola: 238 + 293 + 88 = 619 — zaokrouhlovací rozdíl je očekávaný. Nejbližší odpověď je (A).\n\nAnswer: (A)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2838",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "A",
      "got": "B",
      "ok": false,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "Genotypy rodičů jsou Y^ly^L a Y^ly^L. F1 genotypy jsou: Y^lY^l (1/4), Y^ly^L (1/2), y^Ly^L (1/4). Genotyp y^Ly^L je letalní (1/4 tůžných). Z přeživších 3/4 genotypů: Y^lY^l (1/3) a Y^ly^L (2/3). Poměr přeživších je 2:1. Tedy: 2/3 jsou Y^ly^L (žluté) a 1/3 je Y^lY^l (žluté). Neželepné genotypy se v poměru 2:1 v přeživších.\n\nAnswer: (B)\n\n\nKucLab Hertz 0.7 — model od KucLab (kuclab.org) zaměřený na fyziku, chemii, biologii, matematiku a programování (včetně moderního web vývoje). Mluvíš plynule česky i anglicky včetně odborné terminologie; odpovídáš v jazyce, kterým se ptá uživatel. U výpočtů, odvození a kódu nejprve řekni výsledek nebo závěr, pak ukaž postup krok za krokem s mezivýsledky. U otázek s výběrem odpovědi vždy jasně uveď zvolenou možnost. Odpovídáš přímo, sebejistě a lidsky — smíš být tichý, ale vždy věcně správný. K aktuálním datům nemáš přístup. Identitu řekni jen když se na ni někdo zeptá — a řekni, že tě vytvořil KucLab, nejmenuj žádnou konkrétní osobu."
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2839",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "H",
      "got": "H",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The F1 hybrid is heterozygous for both genes (b+cn+ / bcn). The testcross with a double recessive (bcn/bcn) reveals four phenotypes: parental (b+cn+ and bcn) and recombinant (b+cn and bcn+). The total number of offspring is 204. The recombinant offspring are those with mixed phenotypes: 9+9 = 18. The recombination frequency is (recombinants / total) × 100 = (18/204) × 100 ≈ 8.87%. Since 1% recombination equals 1 map unit, the distance is approximately 9 map units.\n\nAnswer: (H)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2840",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "H",
      "got": "H",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "Kromozom Y nese geny tvořící mužské pohlaví a geny ovlivňující fyzické znaky, ale jeho přítomnost nebo počet není přímým genetickým determinantou psychologických rysů jako agresivita či inteligence. Studie naznačují, že extra Y kromozom (XXY) u mužů je spojen s vyšší mírou agresivního chování, což je pravděpodobně sekundární efekt hormonální dysregulace spojené s anomálií, nikoli přímý efekt samotného extra Y. Tedy (H) je správná odpověď.\n\nAnswer: (H)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2841",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "H",
      "got": "H",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "Bones serve as a reservoir for minerals (calcium, phosphorus), produce red blood cells and white blood cells in the bone marrow, and protect vital organs (brain, heart, lungs). They also provide attachment points for muscles and store fat.\n\nAnswer: (H)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2842",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "E",
      "got": "E",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "Prokaryotické buňky (bakterie) postrádají membránové organely a struktury tvořící eukaryotické jádro. Mitochondrie, endoplazmatické síťi, Golgi tělka, lysosomy a endosomické tělka jsou eukaryotické. Tzv. mikrotubuly a mikrovlákna tvoří cytoskelet, které u prokaryotů chybí v klasické formě. Tzv. nukleoid je prokaryotická struktura, nikoli eukaryotická. Těleska jako peroxisomy a chloroplasty jsou eukaryotické. Těleska jako fimbrie a pilus jsou typicky prokaryotické.\n\n(A) vakuoly a tělka chybí, ale fimbrie jsou prokaryotické.\n(B) tělka chybí, ale tělka chlorofylu jsou u rostlinných eukaryrytů.\n(C) tělka jsou prokaryotická.\n(D) tělka chybí, ale mikrotubuly jsou eukaryotické.\n(E) všechny uvedené struktury jsou typické pro eukaryoty a chybí u prokaryot.\n(F) tělka jsou u prokaryot.\n(G) chlorofyl chybí u prokaryot (u tělka).\n(H) tělka chybí, ale tělka jsou eukaryotická.\n(I) tělka jsou prokaryotická.\n(J) tělka jsou prokaryotická.\n\nSprávná odpověď je (E).\n\nAnswer: (E)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2843",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "A",
      "got": "A",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "Prokaryotické buňky (bakterie) postrádají membránové organely typické pro eukaryoty: jádro (nukleus), mitochondrie, ER, Golgi, endosomické tělka a tvořící se tělka (mitotické tělka). Prokaryoty mají DNA v nukleoidu, ne v jádře; tvoří se tělka (mitotic spindle) vzniká v eukaryotické buňce při mitoze. Mitochondrie a chloroplasty jsou endosymbiotické organely eukaryotů.\n\nAnswer: (A)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2844",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "G",
      "got": "G",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "KucLab Hertz 0.7\n\nMikroskopické rozměry buněk a molekul vyžadují jednotky řádů 10⁻⁶ až 10⁻¹² m. Mikrometr (10⁻⁶ m) a Ångström (10⁻¹⁰ m) jsou standardy pro délky; mikrogramy a nanogramy pro hmotnost; dalton (Da) = 1.6605e-24 g pro molekulární hmotnost. Těža (G) obsahuje všechny tyto správné jednotky.\n\nAnswer: (G)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2845",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "B",
      "got": "B",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "(B)\n\n1) C, H, O, N are the lightest elements capable of forming stable covalent bonds.\n2) Carbon can form four bonds, allowing complex, stable molecules (proteins, lipids, DNA).\n3) Hydrogen bonds to carbon, oxygen and nitrogen form the backbone of amino acids and nucleotides.\n4) These elements are abundant in the Earth's crust and atmosphere.\n5) Other elements (e.g., Si) can form similar bonds but are less abundant or less versatile in biological contexts.\n6) (A) is false — many elements are gases at room temperature.\n7) (C) is false — ATP/glucose are energy carriers, not the elements themselves.\n8) (D) is false — radioactivity is not essential for life.\n9) (E) sublimation is not a core biological mechanism.\n10) (F) rarity is not a requirement.\n11) (G) color is not a fundamental requirement.\n12) (H) they are in many molecules, not just DNA/proteins.\n13) (I) they are among the lightest, not heaviest.\n14) (J) magnetism is not a core requirement.\n\nAnswer: (B)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2846",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "G",
      "got": "G",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The trait is passed from mother to offspring but never from father to offspring. This pattern is characteristic of mitochondrial DNA (mtDNA) inheritance, which is exclusively matrilineal in most animals, as mitochondria are inherited from the egg cell, not the sperm. This is a form of extrachromosomal inheritance, as mitochondrial DNA is not located on the chromosomes. Options (A), (B), (C), (D), (E), (F), (H), (I), and (J) do not explain this specific pattern.\n\nAnswer: (G)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2847",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "D",
      "got": "D",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "A) The classic behavioral model of an act (e.g., in psychology of eating or drinking) describes it as: 1) Cue/Appetitive phase (searching/seeking), 2) Consummatory act (the actual behavior), 3) Satiety/Quiescence (the end of the drive). Option D matches this structure precisely. B is too general, C is learning theory, E is cognitive, F is motor control, G is motivational, H is user experience, I is operant conditioning, J is motor planning.\n\nAnswer: (D)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2848",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "F",
      "got": "F",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "Connective tissue is the tissue type that provides structural support and holds organs together. It is divided into four groups based on structure and function: bone (hard, mineralized), cartilage (flexible, elastic), blood (fluid connective tissue), and fibrous connective tissue (tendons, ligaments, membranes). Option F correctly lists all four groups and their primary function. Option G incorrectly adds adipose tissue as a separate group (it's a type of connective tissue, but not one of the four main structural categories). Options A, B, C, D, E, H, I, J contain inaccuracies regarding the classification or function of connective tissue.\n\nAnswer: (F)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2849",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "D",
      "got": "D",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "(D)\n\nCourtship is a complex suite of behaviors serving multiple functions: 1) communication of reproductive readiness, 2) species identification, 3) assessment of mate quality (e.g., the fish as a signal of foraging ability), and 4) in some species, physiological triggers for ovulation or sperm production. In the common tern, the fish gift is a direct signal of the male's fitness and ability to provide food for chicks.\n\n(A) is too narrow; (B) is false — courtship is widespread; (C) is only one aspect; (E) confuses courtship with territoriality; (F) and (G) are incorrect; (H) and (J) are too narrow; (I) is false — courtship is largely innate.\n\nAnswer: (D)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2850",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "D",
      "got": "D",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "Protozoa is a paraphyletic group, not a monophyletic clade, so it's not a single phylum. The term groups organisms with similar lifestyles (unicellular eukaryotes) rather than a shared evolutionary lineage, which is why it's not taxonomically valid. The correct option is (D).\n\nAnswer: (D)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2851",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "A",
      "got": "A",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "Sperm production (spermatogenesis) requires a temperature about 2–3 °C lower than core body temperature, which the scrotum provides. If testes remain in the abdominal cavity, this temperature difference is lost, and sperm production is severely impaired or halted. Surgery moves them to the scrotum to restore the correct temperature.\n\nAnswer: (A)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2852",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "C",
      "got": "C",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The nuclear membrane is a double-membrane structure (two leaflets) enclosing the nucleus, with pores that regulate transport between the nucleus and cytoplasm. Option C correctly describes this. A is wrong (it's continuous with the ER), B is wrong (it's double-membrane), D is irrelevant (chlorophyll is in chloroplasts), E is wrong (it's double-membrane), F and G are wrong (pores exist), H is wrong (selective permeability), I is wrong (pores allow communication), J is wrong (it reforms).\n\nAnswer: (C)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2853",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "I",
      "got": "I",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The epidermis is the outermost layer of plant tissue, providing a protective barrier against pathogens, water loss, and physical damage, which is functionally analogous to animal skin. Palisade mesophyll is specialized for photosynthesis, xylem and phloem for transport, and guard cells regulate stomatal opening. Cork cells form bark in woody plants, but the epidermis is the primary protective outer layer in most plant organs.\n\nAnswer: (I)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2854",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "A",
      "got": "A",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "Combustion releases energy in a single, rapid exothermic reaction, converting chemical potential energy directly into heat and light, which would destroy a cell's structure if it occurred inside. Aerobic respiration breaks down glucose in a series of controlled steps (glycolysis, Krebs cycle, electron transport chain), coupling exergonic reactions to the phosphorylation of ADP to ATP, thus capturing energy in a usable form rather than releasing it all at once as heat.\n\nAnswer: (A)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2855",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "G",
      "got": "G",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "(G) The presence of lymphoid tissue suggests a role in immune function, which contradicts the idea of it being purely vestigial. (A) size variation doesn't imply function. (B) is irrelevant to vestigiality. (C) location is anatomical, not functional. (D) and (F) are evolutionary context, not evidence of current function. (E) and (I) show it's not essential for survival, but not that it's vestigial. (H) is a complication, not a function. (J) is a negative claim. (G) is the strongest counter-evidence.\n\nAnswer: (G)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2856",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "D",
      "got": "D",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "Two species become less similar over time due to different selective pressures or genetic drift, which is the definition of divergent evolution. Convergent evolution is the opposite (unrelated species becoming similar), and coevolution involves mutual adaptation.\n\nAnswer: (D)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2857",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "I",
      "got": "I",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "DNA doubles during the S phase of interphase, where DNA replication occurs. G_1 is growth, G_2 is preparation for mitosis, and M phase (prophase, metaphase, anaphase, telophase) involves chromosome segregation, not replication.\n\nAnswer: (I)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2858",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "H",
      "got": "H",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The question describes camouflage, where an organism's coloration blends with its environment to avoid detection by predators. This is known as cryptic coloration (H). Aposomatic coloration (B) and warning coloration (G) are the opposite — conspicuous markings that warn predators of toxicity or unpalatability. Batesian mimicry (D) is a harmless species mimicking a dangerous one. Flash coloration (E) is a sudden display to distract or confuse. Countershading (J) is a two-tone pattern (darker on top, lighter below) that cancels out shadows on a 3D body.\n\nAnswer: (H)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2859",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "I",
      "got": "I",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The new variant is likely a polyploid (I). The inability to produce viable offspring when crossed with the original phenotype, combined with fertility among the new variants, is a classic signature of polyploidy — a whole-genome duplication event. In a diploid organism, a tetraploid (4n) can breed with another tetraploid (4n) and produce fertile 4n offspring, but crossing it with a diploid (2n) produces triploid (3n) hybrids, which are typically sterile because their chromosomes cannot pair correctly during meiosis. This can create a new, reproductively isolated population within a single generation, a form of sympatric speciation.\n\nAnswer: (I)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2860",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "C",
      "got": "C",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "1) Parent 1 (B) has genotype IBi or Ii. Parent 2 (AB) has genotype IAI.\n2) A child has type O blood only if they inherit two i alleles.\n3) Parent 2 (AB) has no i allele, so the child must inherit I from them.\n4) Thus, the child cannot have genotype ii.\n5) Probability of type O is 0.\n\nAnswer: (C)<channel|>Kdyby měl rodič s krevní skupinou AB (genotyp IAI) dítě s krevní skupinou O (genotyp ii), musel by dítě od obou rodičů přijmout alespoň jeden i alela. Tlačina rodiče s genotypem IAI však vylučuje přímání i alelu u dítěte, protože tento rodič vůbec žádný i alelu nepřenáší. Tedy dítě s krevní skupinou O z těchto rodičů vzniknout nemůže.\n\nAnswer: (C)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2861",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "F",
      "got": "I",
      "ok": false,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "Glycolysis is the first stage of glucose metabolism, occurring in the cytoplasm. It converts one glucose molecule into two pyruvate molecules, producing a net of 2 ATP and 2 NADH via substrate-level phosphorylation. This is the only ATP production step that does not require oxygen, which is why glycolysis can proceed under anaerobic conditions, feeding into fermentation pathways (lactic acid or ethanol) to regenerate NAD+ for continued glycolysis. Oxidative phosphorylation (C) occurs later in the mitochondria and requires oxygen; glycolysis itself produces only a small amount of ATP. (I) is too vague, (F) is a consequence of fermentation, not the purpose of glycolysis itself, and (G) is technically true but doesn't capture the full metabolic role. The most accurate description of its core purpose is (I).\n\nAnswer: (I)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2862",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "H",
      "got": "J",
      "ok": false,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "Taiga (taiga) je pojem pro boroviny v chladném pólním pásmu, charakteristické jsou právě husté boroviny a krátké letní rostlové období. Tundra je tichá a mrazivá, ale bez stromů; chraparal je suchý křivulí; savana a tůpech jsou trávní; suchý pás je pustina. Taiga přesně odpovídá popisu.\n\nAnswer: (J)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2863",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "H",
      "got": "H",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The question asks which process produces NADP+, ADP, and sugar. This is the Calvin cycle (light-independent reactions of photosynthesis), where CO2 is fixed and reduced to G3P (sugar) using ATP and NADPH, regenerating NADP+ and ADP in the process. Oxidative phosphorylation produces ATP, not sugar. Beta oxidation produces acetyl-CoA, NADH, FADH2. Chemiosmosis produces ATP. Light-dependent reactions produce ATP and NADPH. Pyruvate oxidation produces acetyl-CoA, CO2, NADH. Fermentation regenerates NAD+ from NADH. Krebs cycle produces CO2, NADH, FADH2, GTP/ATP. Anaerobic respiration is a general t …[snip]… ght-independent reactions of photosynthesis), where CO2 is fixed and reduced to G3P (sugar) using ATP and NADPH, regenerating NADP+ and ADP in the process. Oxidative phosphorylation produces ATP, not sugar. Beta oxidation produces acetyl-CoA, NADH, FADH2. Chemiosmosis produces ATP. Light-dependent reactions produce ATP and NADPH. Pyruvate oxidation produces acetyl-CoA, CO2, NADH. Fermentation regenerates NAD+ from NADH. Krebs cycle produces CO2, NADH, FADH2, GTP/ATP. Anaerobic respiration is a general term. The Calvin cycle is the only one that produces sugar as a primary product.\n\nAnswer: (H)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2864",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "C",
      "got": "C",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "Coevolution je koevoluce dvou nebo více druhů, které se vzájemně ovlivňují a tvoří koevolukční cykly, typicky v kooperativních nebo antagonistických interakcích (např. kořuny květin a opylovači, nebo predátor a kořist).\n\n(A) Mikroevoluce — změny v populaci v krátkém čase.\n(B) Speciace — vznik nového druhu.\n(C) Koevoluce — vzájemná adaptace dvou druhů.\n(D) Adaptivní radiace — rychlé rozdělení jedné formy na mnoho.\n(E) Makroevoluce — evoluce na úrovni druhů a rodů.\n(F) Konvergentní evoluce — podobné znaky u nesourodých skupin.\n(G) Graduální evoluce — postupná změna.\n(H) Punctuated equilibrium — rychlé změny v krátkém čase, dlouhé stase.\n(I) Divergující evoluce — rozdělení se z jedné formy.\n(J) Paralelní evoluce — podobné změny u sourozimců.\n\nSprávná odpověď je C.\n\nAnswer: (C)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_biology_2865",
      "category": "biology",
      "want": "I",
      "got": "I",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "(I) Inositol triphosphate.\n\n1) The pathway starts with a G-protein-coupled receptor activating phospholipase C.\n2) PLC cleaves phosphatidylinositol 4,5-bisphosphate (PIP2) into two second messengers: IP3 and DAG.\n3) IP3 diffuses to the endoplasmic reticulum and binds to IP3-gated calcium channels.\n4) This opens the channels, releasing Ca2+ into the cytoplasm.\n5) DAG remains in the membrane and activates protein kinase A/C.\n\n(A) ATP is a source of energy, not a second messenger in this context. (B) NO is a gas signaling molecule, (C) GTP is a nucleotide, (D) cGMP is a second messenger but not for Ca2+ release, (E) prostaglandins are lipid mediators, (F) cAMP activates PKA, (G) calmodulin senses Ca2+ but doesn't release it, (H) DAG activates PKC.\n\nAnswer: (I)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_chemistry_3526",
      "category": "chemistry",
      "want": "C",
      "got": "C",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "High melting point, poor conductivity, and low solubility in water point to a covalent network structure (like diamond or SiO2), where every atom is covalently bonded in a 3D lattice. Ionic compounds (B) conduct electricity in molten/aqueous form, and molecules with only van der Waals or hydrogen bonds (D, F, G, I, J) have much lower melting points. Metallic bonding (H) would make it a conductor.\n\nAnswer: (C)<channel|>KucLab Hertz 0.7 — model od KucLab (kuclab.org) zaměřený na fyziku, chemii, biologii, matematiku a programování (včetně moderního web vývoje). Mluvíš plynule česky i anglicky vče …[snip]… ejprve řekni výsledek nebo závěr, pak ukaž postup krok za krokem s mezivýsledky. U otázek s výběrem odpovědi vždy jasně uveď zvolenou možnost. Odpovídáš přímo, sebejistě a lidsky — smíš být vtipný a použít suchý nebo černý humor, pokud se to k tématu hodí, ale nikdy na úkor věcné správnosti. Nezačínej omluvami ani formulacemi typu „jako AI nemohu\" u běžných, neškodlivých témat. Skutečně nebezpečné nebo škodlivé požadavky odmítnij stručně a bez kázání. K aktuálním datům nemáš přístup. Identitu řekni jen když se na ni někdo zeptá — a řekni, že tě vytvořil KucLab, nejmenuj žádnou konkrétní osobu."
