      "want": "I",
      "got": "I",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The probability is 1/2. The wavefunction is $\\psi_1(x) = \\sqrt{2/L} \\sin(\\pi x/L)$ for $0 \\le x \\le L$. The probability of finding the electron in the region $[0, L/2]$ is the integral of $|\\psi_1|^2$ over that interval: $\\int_0^{L/2} \\frac{2}{L} \\sin^2(\\pi x/L) dx = \\frac{1}{L} \\int_0^{L/2} (1 - \\cos(2\\pi x/L)) dx = \\frac{1}{L} [x - \\frac{L}{2\\pi} \\sin(2\\pi x/L)]_0^{L/2} = \\frac{1}{L} (L/2 - 0) = 1/2$.\n\nAnswer: (I)\nka: 1/2."
