      "category": "chemistry",
      "want": "H",
      "got": "F",
      "ok": false,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The bond energy is 4.4781 eV per molecule. For one mole of molecules, the bond energy is 4.4781 × N_A × e ≈ 447.81 kJ/mol. Since breaking one bond in H2 releases this energy, the bond dissociation energy is 447.81 kJ/mol. This is the energy required to break one mole of H2 into two moles of H atoms.\n\nAnswer: (F)<channel|>The bond energy is 4.4781 eV per molecule. For one mole of molecules, the bond energy is 4.4781 × N_A × e ≈ 447.81 kJ/mol. Since breaking one bond in H2 releases this energy, the bond dissociation energy is 447.81 kJ/mol. This is the energy required to break one mole of H2 into two moles of H atoms.\n\nAnswer: (F)"
