      "id": "mmlu_chemistry_3551",
      "category": "chemistry",
      "want": "B",
      "got": "B",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "Rotational energy levels are $E_J = B J(J+1)$, so transition frequencies are $\\nu = 2B(J+1)$. The difference between adjacent transitions is $\\Delta \\nu = 2B(J+2) - 2B(J+1) = 4B$. The gap between the 2→3 and 3→4 transition is 4B, and between 3→4 and 4→5 is another 4B. The 5→6 transition is 4B higher than the 4→5 transition, and 8B higher than the 2→3 transition.\n1) From $\\nu_{2\\to3} = 2B(3) = 6B = 126.4 \\mathrm{GHz}$, we get $B = 21.067 \\mathrm{GHz}$.\n2) The 5→6 transition is $\\nu_{5\\to6} = 2B(6) = 12B$.\n3) $\\nu_{5\\to6} = 12 \\cdot 21.067 = 252.804 \\mathrm{GHz}$.\nRounding to one decimal place gives 252.8 GHz.\n\nAnswer: (B)<channel|>Answer: (B)"
    },
