      "got": "J",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The final temperature is $T_f = (100+0)/2 = 50^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. The heat lost by the hot block is $Q_1 = m c \\Delta T_1 = 10000 \\cdot 0.385 \\cdot (100-50) = 19250 \\mathrm{J}$. The heat gained by the cold block is $Q_2 = m c \\Delta T_2 = 10000 \\cdot 0.385 \\cdot (50-0) = 19250 \\mathrm{J}$. Since the system is isolated, $\\Delta H = Q_1 + Q_2 = 0$ (heat lost equals heat gained).\n\nAnswer: (J)<channel|>The final temperature is $T_f = (100+0)/2 = 50^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. The heat lost by the hot block is $Q_1 = m c \\Delta T_1 = 10000 \\cdot 0.385 \\cdot (100-50) = 19250 \\mathrm{J}$. The heat gained by the cold block is $Q_2 = m c \\Delta T_2 = 10000 \\cdot 0.385 \\cdot (50-0) = 19250 \\mathrm{J}$. Since the system is isolated, $\\Delta H = Q_1 + Q_2 = 0$ (heat lost equals heat gained).\n\nAnswer: (J)"
