      "id": "mmlu_math_7727",
      "category": "math",
      "want": "F",
      "got": "F",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "(F)\n\nA polygon is any closed plane figure bounded by straight line segments. A hexagon has 6 sides, which is at least 3, so it is a polygon. The other options are false: (A) rectangles are a subset of trapezoids, not vice versa; (B) pentagons have 5 sides, heptagons 7; (C) hexagons have 6 sides, triangles 3; (D) triangles have 3 sides, not less than 4; (E) squares are a subset of rectangles; (G) circles are not polygons; (H) rectangles are a subset of parallelograms; (I) rhombi need right angles to be squares; (J) squares are quadrilaterals, but the reasoning is trivial.\n\nAnswer: (F)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_math_7728",
      "category": "math",
      "want": "H",
      "got": "H",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The total distance is the sum of all four individual distances: 7.04 + 18.81 + 18.39 + 19.94 = 64.18 m.\n\nAnswer: (H)\n\n\nKucLab Hertz 0.7 — model od KucLab (kuclab.org) zaměřený na fyziku, chemii, biologii, matematiku a programování (včetně moderního web vývoje). Mluvíš plynule česky i anglicky včetně odborné terminologie; odpovídáš v jazyce, kterým se ptá uživatel. U výpočtů, odvození a kódu nejprve řekni výsledek nebo závěr, pak ukaž postup krok za krokem s mezivýsledky. U otázek s výběrem odpovědi vždy jasně uveď zvolenou možnost. Odpovídáš přímo, sebejistě a lidsky — smíš být vtipný a použít suchý nebo černý humor, pokud se to k tématu hodí, ale nikdy na úkor věcné správnosti. Nezačínej omluvami ani formulacemi typu „jako AI nemohu\" u běžných, neškodlivých témat. Skutečně nebezpečné nebo škodlivé požadavky odmítnij stručně a bez kázání. Kdy píšeš web kód, vyhýbej se rozpoznatelných „AI slop\" vzorů (generické gradienty, glassmorphism na sílu, klišé texty) — piš čistý, účelný, moderní kód. K aktuálním datům nemáš přístup. Identitu řekni jen když se na ni někdo zeptá — a řekni, že tě vytvořil KucLab, nejmenuj žádnou konkrétní osobu."
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_math_7729",
      "category": "math",
      "want": "A",
      "got": "A",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "Tami's count is 25 + m. Total: 25 + (25 + m) = 50 + m.\n\n(A) 25 + (25+ m) = 50 + m. Správně.\n(B) 25 + m — jen Tami.\n(C) m + 25m = 26m — nesmysl.\n(D) 25m + 25 — m je počet, ne koeficient.\n(E) 25 + 25m — stejné jako D.\n(F) 25m — jen Tami.\n(G) 25m - m = 24m.\n(H) 2(25 + m) = 50 + 2m — Tami tvoří m, ne m tůrka.\n(I) 50 + m — ekvivalentní (A), ale (A) přesněji vyjádří strukturu.\n(J) m - 25 — rozdíl.\n\nVýběr (A) přesně odráží: Ken (25) + Tami (25+m).\n\nAnswer: (A)<channel|>Tami's count is 25 + m. Total: 25 + (25 + m) = 50 + m.\n\n(A) 25 + (25+ m) = 50 + m. Správně.\n(B) 25 + m — jen Tami.\n(C) m + 25m = 26m — nesmysl.\n(D) 25m + 25 — m je počet, ne koeficient.\n(E) 25 + 25m — stejné jako D.\n(F) 25m — jen Tami.\n(G) 25m - m = 24m.\n(H) 2(25 + m) = 50 + 2m — Tami tvoří m, ne m tůrka.\n(I) 50 + m — ekvivalentní (A), ale (A) přesněji vyjádří strukturu.\n(J) m - 25 — rozdíl.\n\nVýběr (A) přesně odráží: Ken (25) + Tami (25+m).\n\nAnswer: (A)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_math_7730",
      "category": "math",
      "want": "A",
      "got": "A",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The shortest distance is 4. Let f(x) = x² + (8/x)². f'(x) = 2x - 128/x³ = 0 → x⁴ = 64 → x = 2.828. Distance d = √(x² + 64/x²) = √(8+8) = 4.\n\nAnswer: (A)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_math_7731",
      "category": "math",
      "want": "E",
      "got": "E",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The dimension of the kernel is 2. The dimension of V is 6 (2×3 matrix space), and since T is onto W, its rank is dim(W) = 4. By the rank-nullity theorem, dim(ker T) = dim(V) − rank(T) = 6 − 4 = 2.\n\nAnswer: (E)<channel|>The dimension of the kernel is 2. The dimension of V is 6 (2×3 matrix space), and since T is onto W, its rank is dim(W) = 4. By the rank-nullity theorem, dim(ker T) = dim(V) − rank(T) = 6 − 4 = 2.\n\nAnswer: (E)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_math_7732",
      "category": "math",
      "want": "G",
      "got": "A",
      "ok": false,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The answer is (A).\n\nThe units digit of 7^n follows a cycle of 4: 7^1→7, 7^2→9, 7^3→3, 7^4→1, 7^5→7, and so on. The exponent 25 modulo 4 is 1, so 7^25 has the same units digit as 7^1, which is 8.\n\nAnswer: (A)<channel|>The answer is (A).\n\nThe units digit of 7^n follows a cycle of 4: 7^1→7, 7^2→9, 7^3→3, 7^4→1, 7^5→7, and so on. The exponent 25 modulo 4 is 1, so 7^25 has the same units digit as 7^1, which is 8.\n\nAnswer: (A)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_math_7733",
      "category": "math",
      "want": "F",
      "got": "F",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "Let w be the width. Then l = 2w. By Pythagoras: w² + (2w)² = (5√5)² → 5w² = 125 → w² = 25 → w = 5. The area is l·w = 10·5 = 50.\n\nAnswer: (F)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_math_7734",
      "category": "math",
      "want": "B",
      "got": "B",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "Let x be the total number of pins. Each pile has x/2.\n1) One-third of one pile is (1/3)·(x/2) = x/6.\n2) Half of that is (1/2)·(x/6) = x/12.\n3) Remaining: x - x/12 = 11x/12.\n4) 11x/12 = 66 → x = 66·12/11 = 72.\n\nAnswer: (B)<channel|>Answer: (B)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_math_7735",
      "category": "math",
      "want": "F",
      "got": "C",
      "ok": false,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "Mean = (98+97+92+85+93)/5 = 465/5 = 92.5.\n\nAnswer: (C)<channel|>Mean = (98+97+92+85+93)/5 = 465/5 = 92.5.\n\nAnswer: (C)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_math_7736",
      "category": "math",
      "want": "A",
      "got": "A",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The two smallest 3-digit primes are 101 and 103. Their product is n = 101 × 103 = 10403. The sum of its digits is 1+0+4+0+3 = 8.\n\nAnswer: (A)<channel|>The two smallest 3-digit primes are 101 and 103. Their product is n = 101 × 103 = 10403. The sum of its digits is 1+0+4+0+3 = 8.\n\nAnswer: (A)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_math_7737",
      "category": "math",
      "want": "F",
      "got": "A",
      "ok": false,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "f(x) = x³ + 2x² − 9x − 18. Derivace f'(x) = 3x² + 4x − 9. Kořeny derivace (kritické body): x = (-4 ± √160)/6 ≈ 1.33 a -2.66. Pro x > 1.33 f'(x) > 0, tedy f rostoucí; pro x < -2.66 f'(x) > 0, rostoucí; mezi nimi klesající. Tedy (A) je správné: pro x ≥ 3 f'(x) > 0, funkce roste. (B) f(x) = (x+3)(x+2)(x-3) → 3 reálných kořenů, (B) špatně. (C) f(0)=-18, f(1)=-14, f(2)=-12, f(3)=0; pro x ≥ 0 minimum v x ≈ 1.33 je f(1.33) ≈ -14.1, takže f(x) ≥ -14.1, (C) správné. (D) f(x) klesá mezi -2.66 a 1.33, (D) špatně. (E) f(x) roste pro x < -2.66, (E) špatně. (F) 3 kořeny, (F) správné. (G) f(0)=-18, f(-1)=-16, f(-2)=-12, f(-3)=0; pro x ≤ 0 minimum v x ≈ -2.66 je f(-2.66) ≈ -14.1, (G) špatně. (H) f(-3)=0, (H) špatně. (I) f(-3)=0, f(-4)=-10, f(-5)=-20; pro x ≤ -3 f(x) ≤ 0, (I) správné. (J) 3 kořeny, (J) špatně.\n\nVšechny (A), (C), (F), (I) jsou pravdivá tvrzení. V tvoříte otázku s jedním správným výběrem? Pokud ne, uveďte všechny správné.\n\nAnswer: (A)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_math_7738",
      "category": "math",
      "want": "C",
      "got": "C",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "Let $d_f$, $d_g$, and $d_h$ be the degrees of $f$, $g$, and $h$ respectively. The degree of a composition of polynomials is the product of their degrees. The degree of the sum of polynomials is the maximum of the degrees of the individual terms. The expression is $f(g(x)) + g(h(x)) + h(f(x))$, so its degree is $\\max(d_f \\cdot d_g, d_g \\cdot d_h, d_h \\cdot d_f) = 36$. We know $d_f = 6$ and $d_g = 3$. This gives three possible terms for the maximum: $6 \\cdot 3 = 18$, $3 \\cdot d_h$, and $d_h \\cdot 6$. Since 18 is less than 36, the maximum must come from either $3d_h$ or $6d_h$. If $3d_h = 36$, then $d_h = 12$. If $6d_h = 36$, then $d_h = 6$. However, if $d_h = 6$, then $3d_h = 18$, so the maximum degree would be 18, not 36. Thus we must have $6d_h = 36$, which gives $d_h = 6$. Wait, let's re-check: if $d_h = 6$, then $3d_h = 18$ and $6d_h = 36$, so the maximum is 36. If $d_h = 12$, then $3d_h = 36$ and $6d_h = 72$, so the maximum would be 72. Thus $d_h = 6$ is the only possibility.\n\nAnswer: (C)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_math_7739",
      "category": "math",
      "want": "C",
      "got": "C",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "(C) is correct. Differentiability at a point implies continuity at that point by definition of the derivative as a limit of the difference quotient. (A) is false: f′(c) ≠ 0 means the function is strictly increasing or decreasing locally, so no extremum. (B) is false: f′(c) = 0 is a necessary but not sufficient condition for an extremum (e.g., f(x) = x³ at x=0). (D) is false: differentiability implies continuity, so a discontinuous function cannot be differentiable. (E) is false: the statement is a contradiction. (F) is false: continuity doesn't imply an extremum. (G) is false: f(x) = |x| is continuous at 0 but not differentiable. (H) is false: f′′(c) = 0 is necessary but not sufficient for an inflection point (e.g., f(x) = x⁴ at x=0). (I) is false: f′(c) = 0 at a single point doesn't make the function constant everywhere. (J) is false: f′′(c) ≠ 0 means the curvature doesn't change sign at c, so no inflection point.\n\nAnswer: (C)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_math_7740",
      "category": "math",
      "want": "D",
      "got": "D",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "1) Start with 9.\n2) Monday: 9 + 17 = 26.\n3) Tuesday: 26 + 22 = 48.\n4) Wednesday: 48 + 3 = 51.\n5) Thursday: 51 + 11 = 62.\n6) Friday: 62 + 18 = 80.\nTotal: 80.\n\nAnswer: (D)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_math_7741",
      "category": "math",
      "want": "E",
      "got": "E",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The product ab is positive if a and b have the same sign. The sample space area is (1 - (-3)) × (4 - (-2)) = 4 × 6 = 24. The region where ab > 0 consists of two cases:\n1) a > 0 and b > 0: a ∈ (0, 1], b ∈ (0, 4] → area 1 × 4 = 4.\n2) a < 0 and b < 0: a ∈ [-3, 0), b ∈ [-2, 0) → area 3 × 2 = 6.\nTotal favorable area = 4 + 6 = 10. Probability = 10/24 = 5/12.\n\nAnswer: (E)<channel|>The product ab is positive if a and b have the same sign. The sample space area is (1 - (-3)) × (4 - (-2)) = 4 × 6 = 24. The region where ab > 0 consists of two cases:\n1) a > 0 and b > 0: a ∈ (0, 1], b ∈ (0, 4] → area 1 × 4 = 4.\n2) a < 0 and b < 0: a ∈ [-3, 0), b ∈ [-2, 0) → area 3 × 2 = 6.\nTotal favorable area = 4 + 6 = 10. Probability = 10/24 = 5/12.\n\nAnswer: (E)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_math_7742",
      "category": "math",
      "want": "G",
      "got": "G",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The triangle is isosceles since one angle is 45° (the other is 45° too). The legs are a = b = 10·sin(45°) = 10·√2/2 = 5√2. Area = ½ab = ½·5√2·5√2 = 25.\n\nAnswer: (G)<channel|>The triangle is isosceles since one angle is 45° (the other is 45° too). The legs are a = b = 10·sin(45°) = 10·√2/2 = 5√2. Area = ½ab = ½·5√2·5√2 = 25.\n\nAnswer: (G)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_math_7743",
      "category": "math",
      "want": "B",
      "got": "B",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "To pass, you need at least 80% of 35 correct: 0.80 × 35 = 28. The maximum number of incorrect answers is 35 − 28 = 7.\n\nAnswer: (B)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_math_7744",
      "category": "math",
      "want": "D",
      "got": "D",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "1) Divisible by 2: 50 numbers (2, 4, ..., 100).\n2) Divisible by 6 (both 2 and 3): 16 numbers (6, 12, ..., 96).\n3) Divisible by 2 but not 3: 50 − 16 = 34.\n4) Probability: 34/100 = 17/50.\n\nAnswer: (D)"
    },
    {
