    {
      "id": "mmlu_physics_9060",
      "category": "physics",
      "want": "A",
      "got": "A",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "1) Heat supplied: Q = P·t = I²R·t = 1.75²·25·100 = 7656.25 J.\n2) Temperature change: ΔT = Q/(m·c) = 7656.25/(0.0825·4186) ≈ 2.22 K.\n3) Final temperature: T_f = 300 + 2.22 = 302.22 K. Nejbližší odpověď je (A).\n\nAnswer: (A)<channel|>Pravděpodobnost, že náhodný člověk vyřeší tuto úlohu správně na první pokus, je přibližně 10 % pro studenta fyziky a 1 % pro běžného človka. To je důvod, proč se fyzika učí.\n\nKrok 1: Výkon ohřevníku: P = I²R = 1.75²·25 = 76.5625 W. Celkové teplo: Q = P·t = 7656.25 J.\nKrok 2: Teprlné změny: ΔT = Q/(m·c) = 7656.25/(0.0825·4186) ≈ 2.22 K.\nKrok 3: T_f = 300 + 2.22 = 302.22 K. Nejbližší odpověď je (A).\n\nAnswer: (A)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_physics_9061",
      "category": "physics",
      "want": "C",
      "got": "C",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The standard Gibbs energy of the reaction is $\\Delta G^{\\circ} = -nFE^{\\circ} = -1 \\cdot 96485 \\cdot 0.222 \\approx -21423 \\mathrm{~J} = -21.423 \\mathrm{~kJ}$. The reaction is $\\mathrm{AgCl}(s) + e^{-} \\to \\mathrm{Ag}(s) + \\mathrm{Cl}^{-}(a q)$, so $\\Delta G^{\\circ} = \\mu^{\\circ}(\\mathrm{Ag}) + \\mu^{\\circ}(\\mathrm{Cl}^{-}) - \\mu^{\\circ}(\\mathrm{AgCl}) - \\mu^{\\circ}(e^{-})$. Since $\\mu^{\\circ}(\\mathrm{Ag) = 0$ and $\\mu^{\\circ}(e^{-}) = 0$ by convention, $\\Delta G^{\\circ} = \\mu^{\\circ}(\\mathrm{Cl}^{-}) - \\mu^{\\circ}(\\mathrm{AgCl})$. Tedy $\\mu^{\\circ}(\\mathrm{Cl}^{-}) = \\Delta G^{\\circ} + \\mu^{\\circ}(\\mathrm{AgCl}) = -21.423 + (-109.71) \\approx -131.133 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$. Zaokrouhli na jednu desetinnou.\n\nAnswer: (C)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_physics_9062",
      "category": "physics",
      "want": "A",
      "got": "A",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The steady-state oscillation is x(t) = A sin(ωt + φ). The rms value of a sinusoidal signal x(t) = A sin(ωt+φ) is x_rms = A/√2. Velocity v(t) = ωA cos(ωt+φ), so v_rms = ωA/√2. Acceleration a(t) = -ω²A sin(ωt+φ), so a_rms = ω²A/√2. All three rms values are proportional to the amplitude A, with the factor 1/√2 coming from the average of sin²(ωt) over a cycle.\n\nAnswer: (A)"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmlu_physics_9063",
      "category": "physics",
      "want": "J",
      "got": "G",
      "ok": false,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "Let t1 be the fall time and t2 the sound travel time. Total time T = t1 + t2 = 2 s.\n1) Fall: h = ½gt1² → t1 = √(2h/g).\n2) Sound: t2 = h/v_sound.\n3) Total: √(2h/32.2) + h/1100 = 2.\nLet x = √h. Then x²/(2·32.2) + x/1100 = 2.\nMultiplying by 64.4: x² + 0.05854x - 128.8 = 0.\nQuadratic formula: x = [-0.05854 + √(0.05854² + 4·128.8)]/2 ≈ 11.316.\nh = x² ≈ 128.06 ft.\nWait, let's re-check the calculation:\nt1 = √(2·128.06/32.2) ≈ 2.826 s.\nt2 = 128.06/1100 ≈ 0.116 s.\nt1+t2 = 2.942 s. Blíže: h ≈ 128.06 ft.\nZadané možnosti: (G) 110.6 ft. Zkusíme t1+t2 = 2 s.\nt1 = √(2·128.06/32.2) ≈ 2.826 s. t2 = 128.06/1100 ≈ 0.116 s. Součet 2.942 s.\nZkusíme t1+t2 = 2 s přesně:\nt1 = √(2h/32.2) → h = 16.1 t1².\nt2 = 16.1 t1² / 1100.\nt1 + 1.464 t1² = 2 → 1.464 t1² + t1 - 2 = 0.\nt1 = (-1 + √(1 + 11.696))/2.928 ≈ 0.964 s.\nh = 16.1·0.964² ≈ 14.96 ft.\nZnovu: t1 = √(2h/32.2) + h/1100 = 2.\nTedy h ≈ 128.06 ft. Nejbližší možnost je (G) 110.6 ft.\nPřepočtáme: t1 = √(2·128.06/32.2) ≈ 2.826 s; t2 = 128.06/1100 ≈ 0.116 s; t1+t2 ≈ 2.942 s.\nTedy h ≈ 128.06 ft. Nejbližší odpověď je (G).\n\nAnswer: (G)"
    },
    {
