      "category": "physics",
      "want": "B",
      "got": "B",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The air in the pump is compressed adiabatically, so T2/T1 = (P2/P1)^(gamma-1). Given P1 = 101.325 kPa (atmospheric), P2 = 24.5 lb/in² ≈ 169.25 kPa, and gamma = 1.40, we have T2 = T1·(P2/P1)^(0.4) = 300·(169.25/101.325)^0.4 ≈ 347 K.\n\nAnswer: (B)<channel|>Answer: (B)"
    },
    {
