      "want": "I",
      "got": "I",
      "ok": true,
      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The recoil energy is E_recoil = E_gamma^2 / 2Mc^2. By conservation of momentum, the nucleus must carry the same momentum as the emitted photon: p_n = p_\\gamma = E_gamma/c. The kinetic energy of the nucleus is K = p_n^2/(2M) = E_gamma^2/(2Mc^2). This is a second-order effect, typically much smaller than the photon energy itself.\n\nAnswer: (I)"
