      "retried": false,
      "raw": "The correct answer is (B).\n\n1) Power: P = V²/R = 240² / 60 = 960 W.\n2) Time in seconds: t = 3.00 × 60 = 180 s.\n3) Energy: E = P·t = 960 × 180 = 17280 J ≈ 1.728 × 10^4 J.\nRounding to two significant figures gives 1.7 × 10^4 J, which matches option (D). Wait, let me re-calculate: 240² = 57600; 57600/60 = 960; 960 × 180 = 17280. Rounding to two significant figures gives 1.7e4. Let me re-check the options. Option (D) is 1.72e4. Let's re-calculate 960 × 180 = 17280. That's 1.728e4. Option (D) is 1.72e4.\n\nAnswer: (D)"
